  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_band_2_cb148bb521d2c9c177ec6fef19fe016b0dd185b2aa8cdf3a2e345af1f38de1c4597">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>the neck-band or collar of a shirt, originally used to make it fit closely round the neck, afterwards expanded ornamentally. Hence, in 16^th and 17^th century, a collar or ruff worn round the neck by man or woman (OED s.v. band n.^2 4a), here made in Flanders | the neck-band or collar of a shirt, originally used to make it fit closely round the neck, afterwards expanded ornamentally. Hence, in 16th and 17th century, a collar or ruff worn round the neck by man or woman (OED s.v. band n.2 4a) | in medieval armor, a sallette is a light globular head-piece, either with or without a vizor, and without a crest, the lower part curving outwards behind (OED s.v. sallet, salade), but the meaning of bandes in this context is unknown</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
